					<description><![CDATA[Fiberglass pocket filters are designed for high-efficiency air filtration in commercial and industrial HVAC systems. These filters are constructed with fiberglass media, which provides excellent particle retention and high dust-holding capacity, making them ideal for environments that require superior air quality.
<ul>
 	<li><strong>Large Dust-Holding Capacity.</strong></li>
 	<li><strong>Sturdy Construction.</strong></li>
 	<li><strong>Fire Resistance.</strong></li>
</ul>]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>High Quality Durable Synthetic  F5 F6 F7 Fiberglass Pocket Filters</h3>
<ul>
<li>This mainly includes F5, F6, F7, and F8 medium-efficiency bag filters, which can be used for intermediate filtration in air conditioning systems.</li>
<li>The frame is primarily made of aluminum alloy or galvanized plate, with a thickness of 21mm or 25mm.</li>
<li>The filter material is melt-blown synthetic fiber, with a V-shaped bag structure.</li>
<li>The inner frame consists of galvanized inner strips and galvanized pressure bars.</li>
<li>The ‘bag support grid’ provides reinforcement to prevent the filter from collapsing or deforming in poor working conditions, and a good hot melt technology</li>
<li>prevents excessive compression or leakage between bags.</li>
